From eea27b4c38cba172283f2a316809b0d014aef2ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yaseen <20190myaseen@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 10:20:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] brokers.html: flagship rebuild on the premium
 partner-landing system
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The shipper page already ran on the pl- design system (aurora hero, live product mock with
floating proof chips, stats band, comparison table, dark step rail). brokers.html was still on
the old generic template — a text-only hero and a three-card row. It now uses the same system
with its own angle so it does not cannibalise free-load-board-for-brokers.html (which stays the
switch-from-a-paid-board pitch):

- Hero: live Load #LB-4471 card showing three real offer states — Accepted (authority active,
  VIN on COI), Passed (posted 6h ago), Blocked (COI expired) — which tells the verification
  story visually instead of claiming it in prose.
- Stats: 15 min offer window / 0 trucks dispatchable without the VIN on the COI / 24 h max age
  of the availability post behind an offer / 1 acceptance closes the load.
- Four gates a carrier passes, the five-step proof chain, and a listing-vs-offer comparison
  table (8 rows) that is the page's strongest asset.
- Portal / email / API section, carrier-network section, 10-question FAQ with schema.

Every claim is an existing product behaviour: the FMCSA authority read, assert_vin_dispatchable,
the 24h availability confirmation shipped this week, first-accept-wins, geofenced stamps.
Verified by rendering the built page in headless Chromium at 1440px and 390px — no horizontal
overflow on mobile.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NLBisLFyx9zVgJDMVRxc9M
